hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21531","Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu 'Uthman, from Ubayy, he said: There was a cousin of mine far in house, and I said: If only you took a donkey or something. He said: It would not please me that my house be joined to the house of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I never heard from him a word more hateful to me than it. He said: And he was mentioning the steps to the mosque. So he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: He has for every step a degree."
"21532","'Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, 'Asim al-Ahwal informed us, from Abu 'Uthman, Ubayy ibn Ka'b narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed you have what you sought."
"21533","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu 'Uthman, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: There was a man in Madinah, I know no man farther than him in dwelling, or he said: in house, from the mosque. It was said to him: If you bought a donkey and rode it in the heat and darkness. He said: It would not please me that my house, or he said: my dwelling, be beside the mosque. So the hadith was conveyed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: What did you intend by your saying: It would not please me that my dwelling, or he said: my house, be beside the mosque? He said: I intended that my coming when I come to the mosque and my return when I return to my family be written. He said: Allah, Exalted, has given you all that, or: Allah has granted you what you sought, all of it, or: Allah, Exalted, has granted you all that, what you sought, all of it."
"21534","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Asim, he said: I heard Abu 'Uthman narrating from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: There was a man who used to come to prayer, and it was said to him: If you took a donkey to protect you from the heat and thorns and stumbling. Shu'bah said: And he mentioned a fourth, he said: Sworn: I do not like that my tent rope be with the tent rope of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So that was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: You have what you intended, or he said: You have the reward of what you intended, Shu'bah says that."
"21535","'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh ibn al-'Anbari narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: My father, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Abu 'Uthman narrated to us, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: There was a man, I know no one among people, among humans, from the people of Madinah who pray the qiblah, farther in house from the mosque than him. He said: He used to attend all prayers with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said to him: If you bought a donkey to ride in the heat and darkness. He said: By Allah, I do not like that my house be attached to the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I informed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he asked him about that. He said: O Prophet of Allah, so that my trace, and my return to my family, and my coming to it, be written. He said: Allah has granted you all that, or: has given you what you sought, all of it, or as he said."
"21536","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, 'Asim narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: There was a man from the Ansar, his house the farthest house in Madinah, and prayer with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hardly ever missed him. He said: So I felt pity for him, and said: O so-and-so, if you bought a donkey to protect you from the heat of the sun and protect you from the vermin of the earth. He said: By Allah, I do not like that my house be by the tent rope of the house of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I carried a load until I came with it to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. So he called him, and he said the like of that, and mentioned that he hopes for reward in his trace. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: You have what you sought."
"21537","Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-'Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu 'Uthman, from Ubayy, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man vaunted tribal pride, so Ubayy made him bite his father's hen, and they said: You were not foul-mouthed. He said: We were commanded with that."
